/**
 * @defgroup MagpGeo MagpGeo — STAR Solenoidal Magnet Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the STAR main solenoidal magnet (MAGP)
 *
 * @details
 * MagpGeo (module name MAGPGEO) describes the geometry of the STAR solenoidal
 * magnet system.  The magnet provides the ~0.5 T longitudinal magnetic field
 * needed for charged-particle momentum measurement.  The model covers:
 *
 * - **Barrel coil** (COIL / MCSE): twelve superconducting coil pairs symmetric
 *   about z = 0.  In setup version 1 each coil is a simplified aluminium tube;
 *   in version 2 a full pancake-by-pancake description is used with aluminium
 *   conductors (5.39 cm × 4.75 cm per pancake), epoxy bonding, and
 *   cylindrical water cooling channels (0.75 cm radius).
 *
 * - **Return yoke** (MRET / MSEC / MBAR): a cylindrical iron shell
 *   (Rin = 303.29 cm, full length 684.40 cm) divided azimuthally into 30
 *   sectors, each containing one trapezoidal iron bar.
 *
 * - **Return rings** (MRGV): two polycone iron rings at ± CoilLen/2 that
 *   connect the barrel yoke to the pole-tip end caps.
 *
 * - **Pole-tip end caps** (MPTV): two polycone iron volumes at
 *   z = ±310.007 cm (inner radius 90.028 cm, outer radius 252.882 cm)
 *   containing the trim-coil cavity (MPCV) and trim coil (MTCL).
 *
 * The outermost mother volume MAGP is a polycone spanning
 * ±357.5 cm in z with outer radius 364.20 cm; it is placed in CAVE inside the
 * MagRefSys coordinate group.
 *
 * ## Setup configurations
 *
 * | Setup name | onoff | magg_version | Description |
 * |------------|-------|--------------|-------------|
 * | MAGPof     | off   | —            | Magnet disabled |
 * | MAGPon     | on    | 1.0          | Simplified single-material coil |
 * | MAGPv1     | on    | 2.0          | Detailed pancake coil with water cooling |
 *
 * ## Volume hierarchy
 * @code
 * MAGP  (PCON/TUBE Air)           — magnet mother, placed in CAVE/MagRefSys
 * ├── COIL  (TUBE Air)            — barrel coil mother
 * │   └── MCSE ×12               — single barrel coil
 * │       └── [v2] PANC  (TUBE Al) — coil pancake conductor
 * │                  └── PAWT  (TUBE Water) — cooling water
 * ├── MRET  (TUBE Iron)           — return yoke cylinder
 * │   └── MSEC ×30 (division)    — azimuthal sector
 * │       └── MBAR  (TRD1 Iron)  — single return yoke bar
 * ├── MPTV ×2  (PCON Iron)       — pole-tip end caps ±z
 * │   └── MPCV  (TUBE Al)        — pole-tip cavity
 * │       └── MTCL  (TUBE Al)    — trim coil
 * └── MRGV ×2  (PCON Iron)       — return rings ±z
 * @endcode
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @file MagpGeo.xml
 * @brief STAR solenoidal magnet geometry (MAGPGEO module).
 * Barrel coil inner radius 264.90 cm, outer radius 299.30 cm,
 * full length 627.40 cm; 12 coil positions mirrored about z = 0.
 * Return yoke outer radius 364.20 cm.  Pole-tip end caps at z = ±310.007 cm.
 * Version 2 adds detailed pancake conductors with water cooling.
 * Author: Pavel Nevski (19 March 1996).
 */

/**
 * @file MagpConfig.xml
 * @brief Setup registry for the STAR magnet detector (MAGP).
 * Defines MAGPof (disabled), MAGPon (version 1, simplified coil), and
 * MAGPv1 (version 2, detailed pancake coil).
 */

